# What tonestress may DO. The speaker, and nothing else -- the same narrow set
# as beep, for the same reason: it exists to prove one thing and a program that
# can only do that one thing cannot be wrong about anything else.
#
# Note what is NOT here and does not need to be: declaring a scheduling period
# is not a capability. Its safety comes from the budget and from admission
# control (kernel/process/process.c, sched_declare_period), not from a gate --
# see the note on sys_sched_period. If it were gated, ordinary programs could
# not ask to be smooth, which is the whole point.

audio
